                                "target_word": "express",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c695a32c-9e61-3c5c-a51c-96f0151bf39f",
                                        "entry_id": "22eede1f-2241-3ecb-a9f0-77a9c31e9e0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To convey or communicate; to make known or explicit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab908fb2-a03e-4f4e-b4f0-17a33254de04",
                                                "sense_id": "c695a32c-9e61-3c5c-a51c-96f0151bf39f",
                                                "text": "Words cannot express the love I feel for him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a571b553-ab0f-4154-b0ce-efdf011c9bee",
                                                "sense_id": "c695a32c-9e61-3c5c-a51c-96f0151bf39f",
                                                "text": "We expressed our readiness, and in ten minutes were in the station wagon, rolling rapidly down the long drive, for it was then after nine. We passed on the way the van of the guests from Asquith. As we reached the lodge we heard the whistle, and we backed up against one side of the platform as the train pulled up at the other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43564090-1938-4e9b-a75a-c3b375c9666b",
                                                "sense_id": "c695a32c-9e61-3c5c-a51c-96f0151bf39f",
                                                "text": "Services during Yom Kippur are held continuously through the day and include readings from the Torah and the reciting of prayers expressing regret or asking for forgiveness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b261b150-0c3b-3bbf-bd36-33f9d5f44d67",
                                        "entry_id": "22eede1f-2241-3ecb-a9f0-77a9c31e9e0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To press, squeeze out (especially said of milk)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bbe5e09-086a-4a2f-b6fa-f088745e7438",
                                                "sense_id": "b261b150-0c3b-3bbf-bd36-33f9d5f44d67",
                                                "text": "The people of his island of Rokovoko, it seems, at their wedding feasts express the fragrant water of young cocoanuts into a large stained calabash like a punchbowl […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe207518-e4c5-47a3-a92d-9b696f4bf5d1",
                                                "sense_id": "b261b150-0c3b-3bbf-bd36-33f9d5f44d67",
                                                "text": "It contained many cysts which were filled with sagolike granules that could be expressed under pressure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba4e79c5-8a42-4c5b-9d4a-6f77957e82b3",
                                                "sense_id": "b261b150-0c3b-3bbf-bd36-33f9d5f44d67",
                                                "text": "They don’t have teats, so the mothers express their milk onto their bellies for their young to feed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74113687-f0b2-304f-b0f4-01e0eac4a602",
                                        "entry_id": "22eede1f-2241-3ecb-a9f0-77a9c31e9e0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To translate messenger RNA into protein."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3565e8ab-a97f-395e-a3ca-9ddaeb3d7b8e",
                                        "entry_id": "22eede1f-2241-3ecb-a9f0-77a9c31e9e0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transcribe deoxyribonucleic acid into messenger RNA."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ee10c6-facb-4d8f-9460-cc48c3a045d0",
                                                "sense_id": "3565e8ab-a97f-395e-a3ca-9ddaeb3d7b8e",
                                                "text": "When a cell “expresses” a gene, it translates the DNA first into a signature messenger RNA (mRNA) sequence and subsequently into a chain of amino acids that forms a protein."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "express",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7455e277-c5be-36c0-b333-afc4e23282ac",
                                        "entry_id": "59158e0f-adcb-3c43-b96a-b8ee424d6326",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of conveying some idea using words or actions; communication, expression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f06dd95-d557-4d45-8a56-efabf19c6b00",
                                                "sense_id": "7455e277-c5be-36c0-b333-afc4e23282ac",
                                                "text": "Whereby they discoursed in silence, and were intuitively understood from the theory of their expresses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2f682b0-b701-3eef-b527-ee8d2c831ca1",
                                        "entry_id": "59158e0f-adcb-3c43-b96a-b8ee424d6326",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A specific statement or instruction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "257a6ffe-3d1a-4495-b66b-d62deac09c2a",
                                                "sense_id": "f2f682b0-b701-3eef-b527-ee8d2c831ca1",
                                                "text": "This Gentleman [...] caused a man to go down no less than a hundred fathom, with express to take notice whether it were hard or soft in the place where it groweth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
